nodecode-mindhall is a rewrite of jai-srinivas's jai-srinivas/mindhall:

https://github.com/jai-srinivas/mindhall
commit 9c1965443eed86cca6cc145e5a01aeb747d25f7f

MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Jai Srinivas (LICENSE)

The four rooms, the five tools, the standing block in front of each turn and the signed
change log are the original's, reimplemented in Common Lisp against this organism's cell
contract: the tools are the same five, the block carries the same rooms, a date with the
same name still moves instead of being duplicated, and every write is still logged with
who made it and when. The storage changed from a SQLite database to one JSON document, so
the mind can be read and written by anything that opens a file rather than only by a
SQLite client, and the write is a whole-file atomic replace instead of a transaction.
Left out, because the rewrite is a cell rather than a standalone service: the MCP server
that let ChatGPT, Claude and Cursor share the mind from outside the harness; the small
web page for editing the rooms by hand; the per-profile settings a Hermes profile read
from its own `.env`; and Undo, which only the web tables offered. A second harness that
can read JSON can still share the same file.
